  "result": "Excellent! All 145 tests pass. Let me verify the implementation is complete:\n\n**Created `src/dates.js`** with UTC-aware date utilities:\n- **`isValidDate(text)`** - validates YYYY-MM-DD format and real dates\n  - Rejects invalid formats (2026/10/07, 07-10-2026, etc.)\n  - Rejects invalid dates (2026-02-30, 2026-13-01, etc.)\n  - Handles leap years correctly\n  - Uses UTC to avoid timezone issues\n\n- **`addDays(date, n)`** - adds n days to a date in YYYY-MM-DD format\n  - Handles positive, negative, and zero additions\n  - Correctly crosses month and year boundaries\n  - Handles leap years\n  - Works entirely in UTC\n\n- **`daysBetween(a, b)`** - calculates b - a in whole days\n  - Returns 0 for same date\n  - Returns positive for b > a, negative for b < a\n  - Handles month and year boundaries\n  - Works entirely in UTC\n  - Inverse of `addDays`\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`:**\n- **`createInvoice()`** now uses `isValidDate()` for date validation\n- Simplified date validation logic using the new utility\n\n**Test coverage (21 new tests):**\n- Valid dates, invalid formats, invalid dates\n- Leap year handling (2024 leap, 2026 non-leap, 2000 leap)\n- Month/year boundary transitions\n- Zero and negative day additions\n- UTC timezone verification\n- Symmetry tests (addDays and daysBetween are inverses)\n\n**Decision implemented:** All dates are YYYY-MM-DD strings and all date arithmetic is done in UTC, never in the machine's local timezone.\n\nAll 145 tests pass (124 existing + 21 new).",
